Kumbhakarṇa rebukes Mahōdara and turns to brother Rāvaṇa --- Kumbhakarṇa vows to wipe fear and make brother carefree --- Kumbhakarṇa mocks timid flatterers who ruined Laṅkā and wasted army --- Rāvaṇa praises peerless friend and sends him to victory --- Kumbhakarṇa lifts all iron spear adorned with garlands --- Rāvaṇa decks Kumbhakarṇa with ornaments armor and blesses him --- Kumbhakarṇa marches with roaring troops though he vowed to go alone --- Kumbhakarṇa swells mountainlike vows to burn hosts slay Rāma Lakṣmaṇa --- Kumbhakarṇa ignores dire omens crosses rampart views cloudlike monkey host --- Monkeys flee like clouds as Kumbhakarṇa roars felling many